---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
<main class="coze-guide">\n  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: title,
    description,
    mainEntityOfPage: 'https://buybetterfinds.com/blog/cozeware-mini-split-buying-guide/',
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Buy Better Finds', url: 'https://buybetterfinds.com/' },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Buy Better Finds', url: 'https://buybetterfinds.com/' },
    dateModified: '2026-10-27',
    inLanguage: 'en-US'
  })} />

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">BUYING GUIDE · HOME &amp; KITCHEN</p>
      <h1>Cozeware Mini-Split Buying Guide</h1>
      <p class="dek">What to know before you buy—from capacity and efficiency to installation, electrical requirements and smart features.</p>
      <div class="hero-offer"><strong>Up to 28% off</strong><span>Use code <b>AWIN99</b> at checkout. Confirm eligibility and expiration with Cozeware.</span></div>
      <a class="button" href={cozewareAffiliate} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer">Explore Cozeware offers ↗</a>
      <p class="disclosure">Buy Better Finds may earn a commission from qualifying purchases made through links on this page, at no additional cost to you.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="creative" href={cozewareAffiliate} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer" aria-label="View Cozeware offer">
      <img src="https://img.yitashop.com/fit-in/800x800/10006/product/original/202605/78108C2A-A060-22E1-5C72-A2AC0BA041FC.jpg" alt="Cozeware mini-split indoor and outdoor air-conditioning units" fetchpriority="high" />
      <span>View the current offer ↗</span>
    </a>
  </section>
  <section class="intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">START HERE</p><h2>What this guide can help you compare</h2>
    <p>Cozeware sells ductless air conditioners and heat-pump systems in multiple capacities and electrical configurations. A lower sticker price does not automatically mean a better fit: the right model depends on the room, local climate, wiring, installation plan and the features you will actually use.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="products" id="models">
    <div class="products-heading"><p class="eyebrow">POPULAR COZEWARE OPTIONS</p><h2>Compare models side by side</h2><p>Model names and listed specifications reviewed against Cozeware product pages on October 27, 2026. Product pages can group multiple configurations; confirm the exact voltage, ratings, included kit and coverage for the selected variant before buying.</p></div>
    <p class="table-hint">Swipe horizontally to compare all columns.</p>
    <div class="comparison-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Cozeware mini-split model comparison table" tabindex="0">
      <table class="comparison-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">Capacity</th><th scope="col">Voltage</th><th scope="col">Efficiency (SEER2 / HSPF2)</th><th scope="col">Published coverage</th><th scope="col">Key features</th><th scope="col">Product</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{products.map((product) => <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a class="model-name model-cell" href={affiliateFor(product.url)} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer"><img class="model-thumb" src={product.image} alt={product.alt} loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><span>{product.name}</span></a></th>
          <td>{product.btu} BTU</td><td>{product.voltage}</td><td><strong>{product.seer}</strong><span class="efficiency-sub">{product.hspf} heating</span></td><td>{product.coverage}</td><td>{product.feature}</td>
          <td><a class="product-button" href={affiliateFor(product.url)} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer">View ↗</a></td>
        </tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="table-footnote">Specifications are summarized from Cozeware's published listings and may change. Where a listing did not clearly establish a specification or coverage estimate, the table says to verify the listing. Coverage figures are not substitutes for an HVAC load calculation. Prices are omitted intentionally; follow each product link for current pricing. Buy Better Finds may earn a commission through these links.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="guide-grid">
    <article><span class="step">01 / CAPACITY</span><h3>Size the room—not just the budget</h3><p>Mini-splits are commonly sold by cooling capacity in BTUs. Cozeware product listings describe different coverage estimates by model, but those estimates are starting points, not a substitute for a proper load calculation. Ceiling height, insulation, windows, sun exposure, air leakage and local climate all affect the capacity required.</p><p><strong>Before buying:</strong> measure the space and ask a qualified HVAC professional to confirm the required capacity, especially for open-plan or multi-room areas.</p></article>
    <article><span class="step">02 / ELECTRICAL</span><h3>Confirm 115V vs. 230V</h3><p>Some models are offered in 115-volt versions while others require 230 volts. Do not assume a unit will work with an existing outlet or circuit. Check the exact model's nameplate, installation manual, minimum circuit ampacity and maximum overcurrent protection requirements.</p><p><strong>Before buying:</strong> have an electrician confirm the available circuit and any required dedicated wiring or breaker.</p></article>
    <article><span class="step">03 / EFFICIENCY</span><h3>Compare ratings on the exact model</h3><p>SEER2 describes seasonal cooling efficiency; HSPF2 relates to seasonal heating performance. Higher ratings can indicate greater efficiency under standardized test conditions, but actual energy use depends on climate, set points, installation quality and how the system is operated.</p><p><strong>Before buying:</strong> compare the precise model's certified ratings and avoid treating broad advertised savings percentages as a guaranteed reduction in your utility bill.</p></article>
    <article><span class="step">04 / COMFORT</span><h3>Check noise, airflow and controls</h3><p>Look at indoor and outdoor sound ratings, fan settings, airflow direction, remote controls, app access and voice-assistant compatibility. Make sure the features listed apply to the specific capacity and series you intend to purchase.</p><p><strong>Before buying:</strong> review the product specifications and user manual rather than relying only on a headline or promotional image.</p></article>
  </section>
  <section class="highlight">
    <p class="eyebrow">INSTALLATION MATTERS</p><h2>Plan the complete project before ordering.</h2>
    <p>A ductless mini-split is more than the indoor unit. Confirm what is included—such as the outdoor condenser, line set, mounting hardware, communication cable, drain components and remote—and what must be purchased separately. Check line-set length, wall penetration, condensate drainage, outdoor-unit placement, electrical work and local permit requirements.</p>
    <p>Refrigerant handling, evacuation, pressure testing and commissioning may require qualified professionals and must follow the manufacturer's instructions and applicable regulations. Confirm the installation requirements for your exact model before assuming it is a simple DIY project.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="installation-budget">
    <p class="eyebrow">BUDGET THE WHOLE INSTALLATION</p>
    <h2>Compare the complete project cost—not just the unit.</h2>
    <p>The product price may not include every item or service needed to get a mini-split running. Before ordering, request an itemized estimate and confirm whether each of these is included:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Electrical work:</strong> dedicated circuit, breaker, disconnect, wiring and any panel upgrades.</li>
      <li><strong>Installation materials:</strong> line-set length, wall sleeve, mounting bracket or pad, drain tubing and weather sealing.</li>
      <li><strong>Labor and commissioning:</strong> mounting, refrigerant-line work, leak/pressure testing, evacuation and startup checks by a qualified installer.</li>
      <li><strong>Permits and code requirements:</strong> local permits, inspections and required outdoor-unit clearances.</li>
      <li><strong>Possible extras:</strong> line-set covers, condensate pump, longer line set, surge protection or difficult-access charges.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Ask the installer to identify exclusions in writing. Never assume a product listing's included-kit image means all installation labor, electrical work or permit fees are included.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="warranty">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">AFTER-SALES CHECKLIST</p><h2>Read the warranty and return terms.</h2></div>
    <div><p>Cozeware's published warranty page lists a <strong>7-year compressor warranty</strong> and a <strong>5-year parts warranty</strong> for air conditioners, subject to its terms. Its return policy says eligible unused items may be returned within 30 days, excludes installed products, and may apply a 20% restocking fee to returns not caused by quality problems. Read the current policies for exclusions, authorized-seller requirements and whether installation labor is covered before ordering.</p><a href="https://www.cozeware.com/article/warranty.html?aid=145" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read Cozeware's published warranty ↗</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="questions">
    <p class="eyebrow">BEFORE CHECKOUT</p><h2>Mini-split buying checklist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Has the room's heating and cooling load been assessed?</li>
      <li>Does the exact model's BTU capacity match the space and climate?</li>
      <li>Is the electrical voltage compatible, with a suitable circuit?</li>
      <li>Have you checked SEER2/HSPF2 ratings and the model's documentation?</li>
      <li>Are installation materials, labor, permits and accessories included in your budget?</li>
      <li>Have you confirmed current price, delivery, returns and warranty terms?</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="cta"><p class="eyebrow">COMPARE BEFORE YOU COMMIT</p><h2>Review the current Cozeware range.</h2><p>Use the product listing to confirm the exact model, capacity, voltage, ratings, included parts and current promotional terms. The public code <strong>AWIN99</strong> was provided in the affiliate invitation as an offer for up to 28% off; verify eligibility and expiration at checkout. Advertised savings are not a guarantee of your energy-bill reduction.</p><a class="button" href={cozewareAffiliate} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer">Explore Cozeware ↗</a></section>
  <p class="fine">Affiliate disclosure: Buy Better Finds may receive a commission if you purchase through qualifying links on this page, at no extra cost to you. This is an informational buying guide, not hands-on testing or professional HVAC advice. Product specifications, pricing, promotions, availability, warranty terms and installation requirements may change. Confirm all details with Cozeware and a qualified professional before purchase.</p>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.coze-guide{--ink:#142b45;--muted:#586675;--navy:#142b45;--blue:#c8102e;--pale:#edf4fa;max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:0 22px 64px;color:var(--ink)}.hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.05fr .95fr;gap:28px;align-items:center;margin:0 calc(50% - 50vw);padding:clamp(28px,5vw,58px) max(22px,calc((100vw - 1136px)/2));background:linear-gradient(105deg,#edf5fc 0%,#f7fafc 47%,#fff 100%);color:var(--navy);border-bottom:1px solid #e1e9f0}.hero-copy{max-width:600px}.eyebrow{font-size:.7rem;font-weight:850;letter-spacing:.16em;color:var(--blue);margin:0 0 15px}.hero h1{font:700 clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4.25rem)/1.02 Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.045em;margin:0 0 20px;color:var(--navy)}.dek{font-size:1.08rem;line-height:1.7;color:#294a68}.button{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:#c8102e;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-weight:850;padding:14px 20px;margin:12px 0;border-radius:4px}.disclosure{font-size:.77rem;line-height:1.6;color:#5d6d7b}.hero-offer{display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin:20px 0 8px}.hero-offer strong{background:#c8102e;color:#fff;padding:9px 12px;border-radius:4px;font-size:.88rem}.hero-offer span{font-size:.88rem;color:#142b45}.creative{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:12px;background:#fff;color:var(--navy);padding:12px;text-decoration:none;font-size:.85rem;font-weight:850;min-width:0;border:1px solid #e2eaf1;border-radius:8px}.creative img{display:block;width:100%;height:330px;object-fit:contain}.intro{max-width:850px;margin:50px auto 30px}.intro{max-width:850px;margin:50px auto 30px}.intro .eyebrow,.guide-grid .step,.highlight .eyebrow,.warranty .eyebrow,.questions .eyebrow,.cta .eyebrow{color:var(--blue)}h2{font:500 clamp(2rem,3.5vw,3rem)/1.08 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.03em;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 14px}.intro p:last-child,.guide-grid p,.highlight p,.warranty p,.cta p:not(.eyebrow){line-height:1.75;color:var(--muted)}.guide-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px}.guide-grid article{border:1px solid #dce5e3;padding:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);background:#fff}.step{font-size:.68rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.14em}.guide-grid h3{font:600 1.45rem/1.2 Georgia,serif;color:var(--navy);margin:20px 0 12px}.guide-grid p{font-size:.94rem}.highlight{margin:44px 0;padding:clamp(24px,4vw,42px);background:var(--pale);border-left:5px solid var(--blue)}.installation-budget{margin:0 0 42px;padding:clamp(24px,4vw,42px);border:1px solid #dce5e3;background:#fff}.installation-budget p,.installation-budget li{line-height:1.75;color:var(--muted)}.installation-budget ul{padding-left:22px}.warranty{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:30px;padding:20px 0 42px}.warranty a{color:#1b6470;font-weight:800}.questions{background:var(--navy);color:#fff;padding:clamp(24px,4vw,42px)}.questions h2{color:#fff}.questions .eyebrow{color:#b7d8d7}.questions ul{padding-left:22px;line-height:1.9}.cta{text-align:center;margin-top:38px;padding:clamp(28px,4vw,46px);background:#f1f5f1;border-bottom:5px solid var(--blue)}.cta p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:780px;margin:0 auto 18px}.cta .button{background:var(--navy);color:white}.fine{font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.7;color:#68757a;margin-top:24px}@media(max-width:760px){.hero{grid-template-columns:1fr}.creative img{height:260px}.product-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.warranty{grid-template-columns:1fr}.guide-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:520px){.coze-guide{padding:0 12px 40px}.hero{padding:24px 20px;margin:0 -12px}.product-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.product-image{height:245px}.guide-grid article{padding:22px}.creative{padding:12px}}
.products{margin:42px 0 48px;width:100%;display:block;clear:both;grid-column:1 / -1}.products-heading{max-width:850px;margin-bottom:18px}.products-heading h2{font:700 clamp(1.9rem,3.5vw,2.6rem)/1.1 Arial,sans-serif;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 12px}.products-heading>p:last-child{line-height:1.7;color:var(--muted)}.table-hint{font-size:.82rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 10px}.comparison-wrap{width:100%;max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto;border:1px solid #d7e1e9;border-radius:8px;background:#fff;overscroll-behavior-inline:contain}.comparison-table{width:100%;min-width:0;table-layout:fixed;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left;font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.45}.comparison-table th,.comparison-table td{padding:12px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid #e1e8ee;vertical-align:middle;overflow-wrap:break-word;word-break:normal}.comparison-table thead th{background:#142b45;color:#fff;font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:0}.comparison-table thead th:nth-child(1){width:22%}.comparison-table thead th:nth-child(2){width:9%}.comparison-table thead th:nth-child(3){width:8%}.comparison-table thead th:nth-child(4){width:15%}.comparison-table thead th:nth-child(5){width:17%}.comparison-table thead th:nth-child(6){width:21%}.comparison-table thead th:nth-child(7){width:11%}.comparison-table tbody tr:nth-child(even){background:#f5f8fb}.comparison-table tbody tr:last-child th,.comparison-table tbody tr:last-child td{border-bottom:0}.comparison-table tbody th{font-weight:700;color:var(--navy)}.model-name{color:var(--navy);text-decoration:none;font-weight:850}.model-name:hover{text-decoration:underline}.model-cell{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;min-width:0}.model-thumb{display:block;flex:0 0 48px;width:48px;height:48px;object-fit:contain;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e1e8ee;border-radius:5px;padding:2px}.model-cell span{min-width:0}.efficiency-sub{display:block;margin-top:4px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.72rem}.product-button{display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;padding:8px 10px;background:#c8102e;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-weight:800;border-radius:4px;font-size:.75rem}.product-button:hover{background:#a30d25}.table-footnote{font-size:.77rem;line-height:1.65;color:var(--muted);margin-top:12px}.products .eyebrow{color:#c8102e}@media(min-width:761px){.table-hint{display:none}.comparison-wrap{overflow:visible}.comparison-table{width:100%;min-width:0;font-size:clamp(.68rem,.72vw,.82rem)}.comparison-table th,.comparison-table td{padding:10px 7px}.model-thumb{flex-basis:42px;width:42px;height:42px;align-self:center}.comparison-table thead th{font-size:clamp(.64rem,.65vw,.74rem)}}@media(max-width:760px){.table-hint{display:block}.comparison-wrap{overflow-x:auto}.comparison-table{width:1100px;min-width:1100px;font-size:.8rem}.comparison-table th,.comparison-table td{padding:12px 10px}}